 "title": "Annular duct in a non-uniform 1/r imposed field (radial: Hartmann walls with variable-field layers, m = 5 and 20; azimuthal: line-current field, conducting walls, and insulating walls with a sliding inner wall): closed forms",
 "physics": "Fully developed 2.5D inductionless flow in 1 < r < 2 driven by G_z (and E_z): radial field B = (C/r) e_r gives axial flow w(r) and an E_z-driven swirl u_t(r) with phi = 0; azimuthal field B = (C/r) e_theta gives w(r) with a radial current K/r closing through the conducting walls, a non-trivial potential and a Lorentz-balanced in-plane pressure; with insulating walls and an axially sliding inner wall (K = 0) the insulating wall carries (u x B).n != 0",
